winhttp: Stub WinHttpSetOption(WINHTTP_OPTION_IPV6_FAST_FALLBACK).

Upstream Wine commit cefdd9ebe60188f3f021d9eb85b0fe7df01ad13a by Hans Leidekker
<hans@codeweavers.com>, 2026-04-09, committed by Alexandre Julliard for wine-11.7.
Carried here for the same reason as 0007: XCurl sets this option on its session, Wine 11.0
fails it with ERROR_WINHTTP_INVALID_OPTION, and the request goes no further
(docs/runtime.md, 2026-09-29). Drop it as soon as the CrossOver sources sake builds are
based on wine-11.7 or later.

The one hunk is placed by hand. Upstream adds the case after
WINHTTP_OPTION_ENABLE_HTTP_PROTOCOL, which session_set_option in the 26.3.0 tree does not
have yet, so here it goes directly before that function's default; the added lines are
upstream's. Left to patch's default fuzz, upstream's own hunk lands in connect_query_option
instead, applies without complaint and stubs nothing.

--- a/dlls/winhttp/session.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/session.c
@@ -279,6 +279,15 @@ static BOOL session_set_option( struct object_header *hdr, DWORD option, void *b
         return TRUE;
     }
 
+    case WINHTTP_OPTION_IPV6_FAST_FALLBACK:
+        if (buflen != sizeof(BOOL))
+        {
+            SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
+            return FALSE;
+        }
+        FIXME( "WINHTTP_OPTION_IPV6_FAST_FALLBACK: %d\n", *(BOOL *)buffer );
+        return TRUE;
+
     default:
         FIXME( "unimplemented option %lu\n", option );
         SetLastError( ERROR_WINHTTP_INVALID_OPTION );
